    "long_instructions": "#### Ethics plays a major role in how AI and computing systems are developed, used, and regulated. As AI becomes more common in everyday life, questions about privacy, fairness, safety, and responsibility become increasingly important.\r\n\r\n<div style=\"background-color: #B7E0E5; border-radius: 10px; padding: 15px; margin: 20px auto; max-width: 85%; box-sizing: border-box; word-wrap: break-word; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 12px; line-height: 120%;\">📖 <strong>Ethics</strong> helps to guide responsible choices about emerging technologies, ensuring privacy, consent, and safety for everyone..</p>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n#### After watching this video, students will explore real-world scenarios where ethical questions arise and consider how different stakeholders—such as developers, users, and affected communities—might view these issues. \r\n\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n#### 🔎 **Think About** \r\n#### As you watch, reflect on:\r\n- #### *What computer system in the video might raise ethical concerns for some people?*\r\n- #### *What are those concerns?*\r\n- #### *How can you deepen students’ understanding of data ethics, bias, or interpretation in future lessons?*\r\n- #### *What strategies will you use to build a bridge between data skills and real-world applications?*\r\n\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 18px; font-weight: bold; background-color: #F5F7F8; padding: 10px; border-left: 5px solid #8148B2; display: inline-block;\">  ➡️ This activity is from Lesson 12. You can find more details in the full <a href='https://studio.code.org/courses/artificial-intelligence-foundations-v2-2025/units/3/lessons/12' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' style='text-decoration: none; font-weight: bold;'>lesson plan</a>.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n"
  },
